Subject: [PATCH 07067/11362] [outer-loop] Task 13: live A/B on
 min_heldout_accuracy relaxed-threshold question

Tests task 11's raised-but-unresolved calibration question directly and
live: does accepting a "good but imperfect" induction (relaxed threshold
0.7) instead of the strict 1.0 bar unlock usable plans the current gate
discards?

Collected real transitions on lp85 (47 collected, 1 real level-up), ran 3
independent fresh real induction attempts (real GPU-backed Qwen3.5-9B-MTP,
min_heldout_accuracy=0.0 to observe the raw held-out score without gate
interference). All 3 attempts scored heldout_accuracy=0.0 -- none landed in
the [0.7, 1.0) relaxed-only band. Honest verdict:
inconclusive_no_attempt_in_relaxed_only_band -- not forced into either
direction.

This null is itself consistent with exp5702's corpus survey: 0.0 is the
single most common real-world outcome (47.4% of the historical corpus),
while the [0.7, 1.0) band is much narrower (~6.3 percentage points), so a
3-attempt sample missing it entirely is unsurprising. Separately disclosed:
despite heldout_accuracy=0.0 on every attempt, plan_reaches_goal=True on
all 3 (in-model verification only, not real ground truth) -- flagged as an
open question, not claimed as evidence the gate is miscalibrated.

First attempt (5 attempts, 1500s timeout) got killed mid-run without
producing output -- cold-starting a fresh llama-server per attempt adds
more overhead than pure inference time. Retried with n_attempts=3 and a
1800s timeout, which completed in 989.5s.

Adds experiment_5704_dynamics_gate_relaxed_threshold_ab.py, its real result
artifact (adversarial_verify clean), 8 tests, REQ-ARC-WMTE-5593-5 spec.md
section, and ops/known-issues.md closure note. The substantive script/
artifact/spec.md content landed via a concurrent conductor checkpoint
commit (d2e9b1d44, byte-identical, verified via git diff) before this
commit -- this commit adds the known-issues.md write-up.

